mind your decisions i'm preshtalwalker  suppose x squared is equal to 17x plus y  and y squared is equal to x plus 17y  if x is not equal to y what is the value  of the square root of x squared plus y  squared plus one equal to  i thank uzla from india for the  suggestion  a similar problem was asked to students  who were approximately 15 years old and  only six percent answered correctly  pause the video if you'd like to give  this problem a try and when you're ready  keep watching to learn how to solve this  problem  [Music]  you might be tempted to solve for x and  y directly  but instead of doing that we will use a  standard trick of manipulating these two  equations  first we'll subtract the second equation  from the first equation  the left hand side is x squared minus y  squared and the right hand side is equal  to 16x minus 16y  we can factor the left-hand side into  the quantity x plus y multiplied by the  quantity x minus y  we can factor 16 on the right hand side  to get 16 multiplied by x minus y  now since x is not equal to y  x minus y is not equal to zero  therefore in this equation we can divide  both sides by x minus y  they'll cancel out and we get x plus y  is equal to 16.  we will then go back to our original two  equations and this time we'll add the  two equations together  we get x squared plus y squared is equal  to 18x plus 18y  this means x squared plus y squared is  equal to 18 multiplied by the quantity x  plus y  but we already know that x plus y is  equal to 16 so we can substitute that in  we then have 18 is equal to 17 plus 1  and 16 is equal to seventeen minus one  we thus get a difference of squares  x squared plus y squared is equal to  seventeen squared minus one squared  one squared is equal to one of course  this is the case if x is not equal to y  from here we add 1 to both sides of the  equation so x squared plus y squared  plus 1 is equal to 17 squared  we then want the square root of this and  this will be equal to 17  and that's our answer  thanks for making us one of the best  communities on youtube see you next  episode of mind your decisions where we  solve the world's problems one video at  a time  [Music]
 

